B1 reuses the B2 architecture end to end: same 22 topics, lesson schema,
Northstar workbook (SEE → CHOOSE → CHANGE → USE → FIX), six-page
fluency-first Live lesson, graders and UI. Only content difficulty changes.

- speakup-b1-blueprint.js: B1 Lessons 1–3 (workbook + Live lessons),
  same grammar focus as B2, shorter texts/sentences, simpler vocabulary,
  lower writing targets
- speakup-b1-northstar-v1.js: installs authored lessons into speakup-b1
  via the shared B2 lesson mapper; unauthored lessons keep current content
- Northstar engine, semantic grading, writing rubric, short-response and
  correction graders now read the level from the lesson ID (B2 unchanged)
- qa:b1 blocking gate for B2 parity and B1 difficulty limits, added to prestart
- B1_LIVING_STANDARD.md

speakup-b1 stays inactive for learners until all 22 lessons are approved.

